<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Charles II, Grand Duke of Mecklenburg-Strelitz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1741–1816</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Charles II, Grand Duke of Mecklenburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strelitz">Strelitz</a>, ruled the duchy from 1794 and was raised to grand duke by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> in 1815. He was a brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlotte-of-mecklenburg-strelitz">Queen Charlotte</a>, wife of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a>, and father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louise-of-mecklenburg-strelitz">Queen Louise of Prussia</a>. He kept his small north German state intact through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars">Napoleonic Wars</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-ii-grand-duke-of-mecklenburg-strelitz.jpg" alt="Charles II, Grand Duke of Mecklenburg-Strelitz" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Georg Ziesenis · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Carl_Ludwig_Friedrich_(1741-1816),_Duke_of_Mecklenburg-Strelitz,_later_Carl_II,_Grand_Duke_of_Mecklenburg-Strelitz.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
